{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jd3kqoPBEZ1uB1xYTYDRFi","type":"tool_result","content":"11:    var asks = function (on) {\n12:      return function () {\n20:    var shown = function () {\n30:   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n31:   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n32:   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n33:   */\n34:  function standAlone() {\n56:  function now() {\n60:  function warn(text) {\n64:  function own(o, k) {\n72:  function json(value) {\n81:  function post(type, fields) {\n91:  function emit(type, args) {\n101:        setTimeout(function () {\n108:  function onMessage(event) {\n118:        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n146:      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n164:  function info() {\n166:    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n172:  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n175:    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n186:    var hello = function () {\n202:  hub.ready = function () {\n209:  hub.answer = function (what) {\n215:  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n219:      setTimeout(function () {\n225:    return function () {\n233:  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n263:  hub.time = function () {\n268:  hub.rng = function (label) {\n279:  function finite(v) {\n284:   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n285:   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n286:   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n287:   */\n288:  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n### 7.12 AI Hub online (`70-hub.js`)\n\nFollow `lib/hub/README.md` (protocol 1, client 1.4.0) exactly. The mode is **ghost**: each copy runs its own race, and\nthe copies send each other only their own car.\n\n1. **Detect.** `AIHub.active` is true from the first line.\n   - Skip the title, menus, attract mode and the touch notice.\n   - Hide **Quit to title**, Restart and Retire (pass `menu.quit: false` at construction), and hide Dev Mode.\n   - The garage and radio are skipped: the car is the Orchidea Spider in seat colour, the song is station 1, the\n     transmission automatic, and the passenger Marisol (chatter Less).\n2. **Connect.** `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it resolves to `null`, boot to\n   the title as normal.\n3. **Prepare.** Build the race for the fixed **Flower Sprint** route (S1 → S2 → S5, ending at a sprint goal arch). Take\n   traffic from `AIHub.rng('traffic')`. Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the boot steps finish, without waiting for a key.\n4. **Our own card (`hubcard` scene).**\n   - **It shows** the title logo over the start line at dawn, the players lined up as cars on the grid in their seat\n     colours with a READY tick, the goal line (\"Fastest to the Flower Sprint goal wins\"), the controls for the last-used\n     device (glyphs), and the countdown from `card.left`.\n   - **Answers.** Enter or ✕ (button 0) or a click on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ (button 3), T, or a click on\n     MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')`.\n   - **Limits.** The card draws from `AIHub.rng('card')` only. It has no settings or choices.\n5. **Start.** On `start`, run the gantry countdown so that GO lands when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`. The sim holds the cars\n   still until then.\n6. **During the race.**\n   - **Clock.** In a session the clock counts **up** (race time). There is no time-out, and the hub's limit ends the\n     round.\n   - **Ghost send, every 100 ms:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: stageId, z, x, v, yaw, drift }, { reliable: false })`.\n   - **Progress, once a second:** `AIHub.progress({ score: metres along the route, label: 'Stage 2/3 · 64%' })`. Start\n     both the sends and the progress at `start`, even while the score is still 0: the harness only pokes random keys,\n     yet checks that every copy sends and reports.\n   - **Ghost cars.** Others are drawn as translucent cars in their seat colour with name tags (the pixel font; any\n     glyph it lacks becomes `?`; never HTML), only while they share our `area`, smoothed toward their last state. A\n     standings strip on the HUD shows everyone's progress.\n7. **Goal.** `AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time()) })`, plus `send({ t: 'done', time })` and\n   `stats: { 'Best drift': …, 'Near misses': … }`. Then keep cruising behind a \"Waiting for the others…\" banner while\n   the ghosts keep coming.\n8. **Endings.**\n   - **`time-up`:** if the race is still going, `AIHub.result({ score: metres })` at once.\n   - **`end`:** stop taking input, `stopMusic`, fade the engine loops and mute all audio, freeze the sim, and show\n     \"Round over\" until the hub removes the page.\n   - **`leave`:** drop that player's ghost.\n9. **Hard rules in a session.** No network except through the hub. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or\n   navigation. The pause menu offers Resume, Settings and Controls only. Options is ignored while Create is held (E4).\n   The empty storage the client provides means a fresh profile, which is fine.\n\n### 7.13 Characters and animation (`12-cast.js`)\n\nAll characters are engine `E.Humanoid` rigs dressed per §8.5, animated by the rig's own system: poses, expressions,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"98d2eee2-be21-406a-ab47-2d9a90993c94","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:22:46.430Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"11:    var asks = function (on) {\n12:      return function () {\n20:    var shown = function () {\n30:   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n31:   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n32:   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n33:   */\n34:  function standAlone() {\n56:  function now() {\n60:  function warn(text) {\n64:  function own(o, k) {\n72:  function json(value) {\n81:  function post(type, fields) {\n91:  function emit(type, args) {\n101:        setTimeout(function () {\n108:  function onMessage(event) {\n118:        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n146:      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n164:  function info() {\n166:    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n172:  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n175:    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n186:    var hello = function () {\n202:  hub.ready = function () {\n209:  hub.answer = function (what) {\n215:  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n219:      setTimeout(function () {\n225:    return function () {\n233:  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n263:  hub.time = function () {\n268:  hub.rng = function (label) {\n279:  function finite(v) {\n284:   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n285:   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n286:   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n287:   */\n288:  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n### 7.12 AI Hub online (`70-hub.js`)\n\nFollow `lib/hub/README.md` (protocol 1, client 1.4.0) exactly. The mode is **ghost**: each copy runs its own race, and\nthe copies send each other only their own car.\n\n1. **Detect.** `AIHub.active` is true from the first line.\n   - Skip the title, menus, attract mode and the touch notice.\n   - Hide **Quit to title**, Restart and Retire (pass `menu.quit: false` at construction), and hide Dev Mode.\n   - The garage and radio are skipped: the car is the Orchidea Spider in seat colour, the song is station 1, the\n     transmission automatic, and the passenger Marisol (chatter Less).\n2. **Connect.** `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it resolves to `null`, boot to\n   the title as normal.\n3. **Prepare.** Build the race for the fixed **Flower Sprint** route (S1 → S2 → S5, ending at a sprint goal arch). Take\n   traffic from `AIHub.rng('traffic')`. Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the boot steps finish, without waiting for a key.\n4. **Our own card (`hubcard` scene).**\n   - **It shows** the title logo over the start line at dawn, the players lined up as cars on the grid in their seat\n     colours with a READY tick, the goal line (\"Fastest to the Flower Sprint goal wins\"), the controls for the last-used\n     device (glyphs), and the countdown from `card.left`.\n   - **Answers.** Enter or ✕ (button 0) or a click on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ (button 3), T, or a click on\n     MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')`.\n   - **Limits.** The card draws from `AIHub.rng('card')` only. It has no settings or choices.\n5. **Start.** On `start`, run the gantry countdown so that GO lands when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`. The sim holds the cars\n   still until then.\n6. **During the race.**\n   - **Clock.** In a session the clock counts **up** (race time). There is no time-out, and the hub's limit ends the\n     round.\n   - **Ghost send, every 100 ms:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: stageId, z, x, v, yaw, drift }, { reliable: false })`.\n   - **Progress, once a second:** `AIHub.progress({ score: metres along the route, label: 'Stage 2/3 · 64%' })`. Start\n     both the sends and the progress at `start`, even while the score is still 0: the harness only pokes random keys,\n     yet checks that every copy sends and reports.\n   - **Ghost cars.** Others are drawn as translucent cars in their seat colour with name tags (the pixel font; any\n     glyph it lacks becomes `?`; never HTML), only while they share our `area`, smoothed toward their last state. A\n     standings strip on the HUD shows everyone's progress.\n7. **Goal.** `AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time()) })`, plus `send({ t: 'done', time })` and\n   `stats: { 'Best drift': …, 'Near misses': … }`. Then keep cruising behind a \"Waiting for the others…\" banner while\n   the ghosts keep coming.\n8. **Endings.**\n   - **`time-up`:** if the race is still going, `AIHub.result({ score: metres })` at once.\n   - **`end`:** stop taking input, `stopMusic`, fade the engine loops and mute all audio, freeze the sim, and show\n     \"Round over\" until the hub removes the page.\n   - **`leave`:** drop that player's ghost.\n9. **Hard rules in a session.** No network except through the hub. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or\n   navigation. The pause menu offers Resume, Settings and Controls only. Options is ignored while Create is held (E4).\n   The empty storage the client provides means a fresh profile, which is fine.\n\n### 7.13 Characters and animation (`12-cast.js`)\n\nAll characters are engine `E.Humanoid` rigs dressed per §8.5, animated by the rig's own system: poses, expressions,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jd3kqoPBEZ1uB1xYTYDRFi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghoT6M3AkN4neeUD84RQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016gyz3TJ7nnSmxqgAtHCEL3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-042140__xe1b7e1/work/dev; sed -n 290,330p vendor/hub/session.js; sed -n 395,520p vendor/hub/session.js; grep -n \"^  hub\\.\\|^   \\* \" vendor/hub/session.js | head -0; sed -n 1,200p engine/modules/road.js | cut -c1-240"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2284,"cache_read_input_tokens":64285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2284},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"9eb363d5-efac-42a7-aaa0-d3bf6be075c9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:22:50.577Z","request_id":"req_011CghoT63gQQXbTE2X1EVRK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016gyz3TJ7nnSmxqgAtHCEL3":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-042140__xe1b7e1/work/dev; sed -n 290,330p vendor/hub/session.js; sed -n 395,520p vendor/hub/session.js; grep -n \"^  hub\\.\\|^   \\* \" vendor/hub/session.js | head -0; sed -n 1,200p engine/modules/road.js | cut -c1-240"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016gyz3TJ7nnSmxqgAtHCEL3","type":"tool_result","content":"  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n  };\n\n  /** A number the hub can rank: finite, given as a number or as text. Not null, '' or true, which JSON or Number would make 0. */\n  function finite(v) {\n    return (typeof v === 'number' || (typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '')) && isFinite(v);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The whole outcome as plain JSON, field by field: the hub checks and trims\n   * it, so new optional fields need no new client. A field that is not JSON\n   * (a cycle, a BigInt) is left out, not the whole outcome.\n   */\n  function outcomeOf(outcome) {\n    if (!outcome || typeof outcome !== 'object' || Array.isArray(outcome)) {\n      warn('the outcome is not a plain object');\n      return null;\n    }\n    var copy = {};\n    for (var key in outcome) {\n      if (!own(outcome, key)) continue;\n      var value = json(outcome[key]);\n      if (value !== undefined) copy[key] = value;\n      else if (outcome[key] !== undefined) warn('the outcome\\'s ' + key + ' is not JSON: left out');\n    }\n    return copy;\n  }\n\n  /** Race and side by side: report your own outcome once, {time: ms} (lower wins) or {score: n} (higher wins), with optional stats and awards. */\n  hub.result = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    var given = outcome || {};\n    delete fields.time;\n    delete fields.score;\n    if (finite(given.time)) fields.time = Number(given.time);\n    if (finite(given.score)) fields.score = Number(given.score);\n    if (!own(fields, 'time') && !own(fields, 'score')) return warn('result needs a finite time or score');\n    reported = true;\n    if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n    post('result', fields);\n  };\n\n  /** Versus and co-op: the host reports the standings once, best first, ties grouped: [[2], [0, 3], [1]]. */\n  hub.finish = function (outcome) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported) return;\n    if (!hub.isHost) return warn('finish is for the host only');\n    var fields = outcomeOf(outcome);\n    if (!fields) return;\n    if (!Array.isArray(fields.standings)) return warn('finish needs standings');\n    reported = true;\n    post('finish', fields);\n  };\n\n  function sendProgress() {\n    progressTimer = null;\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\n    lastProgress = now();\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\n    nextProgress = null;\n  }\n\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\n  };\n\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\n  };\n\n  hub.inspect = function () {\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\n    try {\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\n    } catch (e) {\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\n    }\n  };\n\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\n    if (!hub.active) return;\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\n  };\n\n  root.AIHub = hub;\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ROAD v0.85.2: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color' }).\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\n\n```js road\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\n```\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\nclass Road {\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ segment: 200, width: 2000, lanes: 3, rumble: 3, draw: 240, fov: 100, height: 1000, fog: { color: '#a0c0e0', density: 5 }, sky: '#6aa8e8' }, o);\n    this.o.colors = Object.assign({}, COLORS, o.colors);\n    /** segs: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things }); length: the lap in world units; depth: the\n     *  camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width) */\n    this.segs = []; this.length = 0; this.depth = 1 / Math.tan(this.o.fov / 2 * Math.PI / 180);\n    this._cam = null; this._out = null;\n  }\n  /** n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors */\n  add(n, o = {}) {\n    const y0 = this.segs.length ? this.segs[this.segs.length - 1].y1 : 0, curve = o.curve || 0, hill = o.hill || 0, e = Math.max(1, Math.min(n / 3, 25)), L = this.o.segment;\n    for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n      const c = k < e ? easeIn(0, curve, k / e) : k > n - e ? easeInOut(curve, 0, (k - (n - e)) / e) : curve, i = this.segs.length;\n      this.segs.push({ i, z: i * L, y0: easeInOut(y0, y0 + hill, k / n), y1: easeInOut(y0, y0 + hill, (k + 1) / n), curve: c, tunnel: !!o.tunnel, colors: o.colors || null, things: [] });\n    }\n    this.length = this.segs.length * this.o.segment; return this;\n  }\n  /** the segment at a distance (it wraps) */\n  seg(z) { const n = this.segs.length; return this.segs[((Math.floor(z / this.o.segment) % n) + n) % n]; }\n  /** scenery at distance z, offset across: what = an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or { draw(g,\n   *  sx, sy, scale), w } */\n  place(z, offset, what, scale = 8) {\n    const spr = what.isAnim ? what.frames[0] : what.isSprite ? what : null;\n    this.seg(z).things.push({ offset, what, scale, w: spr ? spr.w * scale : what.w || 200 }); return this;\n  }\n  /** how hard the road bends at a distance */\n  curveAt(z) { return this.seg(z).curve; }\n  /** the road's height at a distance */\n  yAt(z) { const L = this.o.segment, s = this.seg(z), u = ((z % L) + L) % L / L; return s.y0 + (s.y1 - s.y0) * u; }\n  /** the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches */\n  hits(z, x, w) { const W = this.o.width; return this.seg(z).things.filter(t => Math.abs(t.offset - x) * W < t.w / 2 + w * W); }\n  /** how far past the camera the player's car stands when drawn at the screen's bottom, for a camera h over the road */\n  ahead(h = this.o.height) { return h * this.depth; }\n  // a road point into the screen for camera C: { x, y, w (half the road there, pixels), scale (pixels a unit), d }\n  _p(wx, wy, wz, C) {\n    const d = wz - C.z; if (d <= 0) return null;\n    const s = this.depth / d; return { x: C.cx + s * (wx - C.x) * C.hw, y: C.cy - s * (wy - C.y) * C.hh, w: s * this.o.width * C.hw, scale: s * C.hw, d };\n  }\n  /** a point (distance z, across x in half roads, height y over the road) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera last drawn,\n   *  or null behind it */\n  project(z, x, y = 0) {\n    const C = this._cam; if (!C) return null;\n    let dz = z - C.z; if (dz < 0) dz += this.length;\n    const L = this.o.segment, u = dz / L + C.pct, k = Math.floor(u), B = C.bend, b = k + 1 < B.length ? B[k] + (B[k + 1] - B[k]) * (u - k) : B[B.length - 1] || 0;\n    const p = this._p(x * this.o.width + b, this.yAt(z) + y, C.z + dz, C); return p && [p.x, p.y, p.scale];\n  }\n  /** draw the road over r's frame (an overlay; r.viewport's part in a split screen): { z, x, h, turn, cars } */\n  draw(r, v = {}) {\n    const vp = r.viewport || { x: 0, y: 0, w: r.bw, h: r.bh }, o = this.o, segs = this.segs, n = segs.length, L = o.segment, cars = v.cars || [];\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      const W = vp.w, H = vp.h, z = ((v.z || 0) % this.length + this.length) % this.length, base = this.seg(z), pct = (z % L) / L, t = r.game.time;\n      const C = this._cam = { x: (v.x || 0) * o.width, y: (v.h === undefined ? o.height : v.h) + this.yAt(z), z, cx: vp.x + W / 2, cy: vp.y + H / 2, hw: W / 2, hh: H / 2, pct, bend: [] };\n      const out = this._out && this._out.width === W && this._out.height === H ? this._out : (this._out = E.mkCanvas(W, H)), cg = E.ctx2d(out);\n      cg.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, -vp.x, -vp.y);\n      if (o.sky && o.sky.draw) { const val = value => ({ value }); o.sky.draw(Object.create(r, { ctx: val(cg), bw: val(W), bh: val(H), W: val(W), H: val(H), ix: val(v.turn || 0), iy: val(0) })); }\n      else E.px.rect(cg, vp.x, vp.y, W, H, o.sky || '#6aa8e8');\n      // near to far: each segment projected, bending as the curves add up; it shows only above the last one shown (a\n      // crest hides the road past it)\n      const list = []; let maxy = vp.y + H, x = 0, dx = -(base.curve * pct);\n      for (let k = 0; k < Math.min(o.draw, n); k++) {\n        const s = segs[(base.i + k) % n], wz = s.z + (s.i < base.i ? this.length : 0);\n        C.bend.push(x);\n        const p1 = this._p(x, s.y0, wz, C), p2 = this._p(x + dx, s.y1, wz + L, C), show = !!(p1 && p2 && p1.d > this.depth && p2.y < p1.y && p2.y < maxy);\n        x += dx; dx += s.curve; list.push([s, p1, p2, show, wz]); if (show) maxy = p2.y;\n      }\n      C.bend.push(x);\n      // far to near: the road under each segment, then what stands on it (nearer road covers what a crest hides)\n      const fog = o.fog && E.hex(o.fog.color), byseg = new Map();\n      for (const c of cars) { const s = this.seg(c.z); (byseg.get(s) || byseg.set(s, []).get(s)).push(c); }\n      for (let k = list.length - 1; k > 0; k--) {\n        const [s, p1, p2, show, wz] = list[k], f = fog ? 1 - Math.exp(-((k / o.draw) ** 2) * o.fog.density) : 0;\n        if (show) this._band(cg, vp, s, p1, p2, fog, f);\n        const things = s.things, cs = byseg.get(s); if (!p1 || (!things.length && !cs)) continue;\n        cg.globalAlpha = 1 - f * .8;\n        for (const th of things) this._thing(cg, th.what, p1.x + p1.scale * th.offset * o.width, p1.y, p1.scale, th.scale, t);\n        if (cs) for (const c of cs) {   // a car between its segment's ends\n          const u = (((c.z - wz) % this.length + this.length) % this.length) / L, q = p2 || p1, sc = p1.scale + (q.scale - p1.scale) * u;\n          this._thing(cg, c, p1.x + (q.x - p1.x) * u + sc * c.x * o.width, p1.y + (q.y - p1.y) * u, sc, 8, t);\n        }\n        cg.globalAlpha = 1;\n      }\n      cg.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0); g.drawImage(out, vp.x, vp.y);\n    });\n    return this;\n  }\n  // a thing at its foot (sx, sy), scale pixels a unit: a sprite or anim (spr world units a pixel), or its own draw\n  _thing(g, q, sx, sy, scale, spr, t) {\n    E.px.reset(g);   // (the color cache forgotten: the fog and the alpha set the canvas directly)\n    if (q.draw) return q.draw(g, sx, sy, scale);\n    const sp = q.isAnim ? q.frame(t) : q, k = scale * spr, w = sp.w * k, h = sp.h * k; if (w < .5) return;\n    g.drawImage(sp.cv, Math.round(sx - w / 2), Math.round(sy - h), Math.max(1, Math.round(w)), Math.max(1, Math.round(h)));\n  }\n  // a segment's band: the grass across, the rumble strips, the road and its lanes; a tunnel's walls and roof; the fog\n  _band(g, vp, s, p1, p2, fog, f) {\n    const o = this.o, px = E.px, C = s.colors ? Object.assign({}, o.colors, s.colors) : o.colors, alt = Math.floor(s.i / o.rumble) % 2, W = vp.w, X = vp.x, y1 = Math.ceil(p1.y), y2 = Math.ceil(p2.y);   // (the rows its polygons fill: from p\n    const quad = (x1, w1, x2, w2, c) => px.poly(g, [[x1 - w1, p1.y], [x1 + w1, p1.y], [x2 + w2, p2.y], [x2 - w2, p2.y]], c);\n    px.rect(g, X, y2, W, y1 - y2, C.grass[alt]);\n    const k = Math.max(6, 2 * o.lanes);\n    quad(p1.x, p1.w * (1 + 1 / k), p2.x, p2.w * (1 + 1 / k), C.rumble[alt]);\n    quad(p1.x, p1.w, p2.x, p2.w, C.road[alt]);\n    if (!alt) for (let l = 1; l < o.lanes; l++) { const u = -1 + 2 * l / o.lanes; quad(p1.x + u * p1.w, p1.w / (16 * o.lanes), p2.x + u * p2.w, p2.w / (16 * o.lanes), C.lane); }\n    if (s.tunnel) {   // walls from beyond the rumble up to a roof; where it starts, a face round its mouth\n      const e1 = p1.w * 1.25, e2 = p2.w * 1.25, t1 = p1.y - p1.w * .8, t2 = p2.y - p2.w * .8, n = this.segs.length;\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x - e1, p1.y], [p2.x - e2, p2.y], [p2.x - e2, t2], [p1.x - e1, t1]], C.wall[alt]);\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x + e1, p1.y], [p2.x + e2, p2.y], [p2.x + e2, t2], [p1.x + e1, t1]], C.wall[alt]);\n      px.poly(g, [[p1.x - e1, t1], [p1.x + e1, t1], [p2.x + e2, t2], [p2.x - e2, t2]], C.roof);\n      if (!this.segs[(s.i + n - 1) % n].tunnel) {\n        const a = Math.round(p1.x - e1), b = Math.round(p1.x + e1), top = clamp(Math.round(t1), vp.y, y1), r = X + W;\n        px.rect(g, X, vp.y, W, top - vp.y, C.portal); if (a > X) px.rect(g, X, top, Math.min(a, r) - X, y1 - top, C.portal); if (b < r) px.rect(g, Math.max(b, X), top, r - Math.max(b, X), y1 - top, C.portal);\n      }\n    }\n    if (f > .01) { g.fillStyle = `rgba(${fog[0]},${fog[1]},${fog[2]},${f.toFixed(3)})`; g.fillRect(X, y2, W, y1 - y2); px.reset(g); }   // fog thickening with the distance\n  }\n}\nE.Road = Road;\n})(typeof My3D2dge !== 'undefined' ? M