{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghobK6UYXwfwr2BjA8GL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012Mmcd1k8fhq8xLTTPXsVsc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-042140__xe1b7e1/work/dev/engine; sed -n 1,40p kits/test.mjs | cut -c1-250; sed -n 1,60p game/game.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"store = {\" -A12 my-3d2dge.js | head -20"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"cache_read_input_tokens":111053,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2520},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"3484c2b4-5bce-4918-947c-ab484209f889","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:25:27.529Z","request_id":"req_011CghobJo7nDRTVbMbukweX","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012Mmcd1k8fhq8xLTTPXsVsc":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-042140__xe1b7e1/work/dev/engine; sed -n 1,40p kits/test.mjs | cut -c1-250; sed -n 1,60p game/game.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"store = {\" -A12 my-3d2dge.js | head -20"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Mmcd1k8fhq8xLTTPXsVsc","type":"tool_result","content":"// A headless test of the genre kits: each kit's game runs in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where there is no\n// DOM) after the scripts its page loads before it (the engine, an asset set), starts its slice (the page's deep link,\n// #<id>), plays two seconds, then runs the slice's proof twice: run(600), scripted play from a seed, gives a hash of how\n// it went, the same every time. Run it: node kits/test.mjs [id ...] (every kit without one; exit code 1 on a failure).\n// A game copied from a kit tests the same way: a kit's code reads three of the page's globals, given stand-ins here\n// (window, addEventListener, location); drive it with game.advance and input.tap / hold, as game/test.mjs does.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst here = new URL('./', import.meta.url), read = f => readFileSync(new URL(f, here), 'utf8');\nconst ids = process.argv.slice(2).length ? process.argv.slice(2) : readdirSync(here).filter(f => f.endsWith('.html')).map(f => f.slice(0, -5)).sort();\nlet failed = 0;\nfor (const id of ids) {\n  const ctx = { console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error: console.error }, addEventListener() {}, location: { hash: '#' + id } };\n  ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);\n  try {\n    // the page's scripts, in its order: ../my-3d2dge.js, any asset set, then the kit's game\n    for (const [, src] of read(id + '.html').matchAll(/<script src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>/g)) vm.runInContext(read(src), ctx, { filename: src });\n    const game = ctx.My3D2dge.current, slice = ctx.__game.scenes[id];\n    game.advance(2);\n    const scene = game.sceneName, a = slice.run(600), b = slice.run(600), errors = game.errors.map(e => e.message), ok = a === b && !errors.length;\n    console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + id + ': ' + scene + ' plays; its proof twice ' + (a === b ? 'the same (' + a + ')' : a + ', then ' + b) + (errors.length ? '; errors: ' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\n    if (!ok) failed++;\n  } catch (e) { console.log('FAIL ' + id + ': ' + (e && e.stack || e).toString().split('\\n').slice(0, 3).join(' / ')); failed++; }\n}\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} of ${ids.length} kit(s) failed` : `all ${ids.length} kit(s) passed`);\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n301:const store = {\n302-  get(key, fallback = null) { try { const v = localStorage.getItem('my3d2dge:' + key); return v === null ? fallback : JSON.parse(v); } catch (e) { return fallback; } },   // the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n303-  set(key, value) { try { localStorage.setItem('my3d2dge:' + key, JSON.stringify(value)); return true; } catch (e) { return false; } },   // save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n304-  remove(key) { try { localStorage.removeItem('my3d2dge:' + key); } catch (e) { /* storage blocked */ } }   // forget key\n305-};\n306-Object.assign(E, { clamp, lerp, approach, ease, wrap, wrapDiff, angDiff, lerpAng, approachAng, rng, hash2, noise2, bayer, smoothDamp, hex, toHex, shade, mix, mkCanvas, ctx2d, V3, ik3,\n307-  rand, randInt, pick, chance, dist, angleTo, arc, overlap, overlapBox, inArc, sameLevel, targets, HEIGHTS, prune, store });\n308-\n309-/* the ways in for the core's sections a kit may leave out (the kit diet: sprite turns, tweens, scripts, transitions,\n310-   weather, input sequences, the camera's window): each puts its functions here as it loads, so a kit without it has\n311-   nothing to call. input(game, dt) after the input's step, step(game, dt) after the timers (game time: paused, frozen\n312-   and slowed with the game), enter(game, old) as a scene starts (before its enter), draw(game, r, g) over the lit\n313-   world, under the overlays; rot(spr, a, steps): a sprite turned (section 2b); frame(game, shx, shy): a split screen's","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"daf3bac5-5b27-4c6b-af32-ee8b1761fa88","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:25:27.547Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// A headless test of the genre kits: each kit's game runs in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where there is no\n// DOM) after the scripts its page loads before it (the engine, an asset set), starts its slice (the page's deep link,\n// #<id>), plays two seconds, then runs the slice's proof twice: run(600), scripted play from a seed, gives a hash of how\n// it went, the same every time. Run it: node kits/test.mjs [id ...] (every kit without one; exit code 1 on a failure).\n// A game copied from a kit tests the same way: a kit's code reads three of the page's globals, given stand-ins here\n// (window, addEventListener, location); drive it with game.advance and input.tap / hold, as game/test.mjs does.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst here = new URL('./', import.meta.url), read = f => readFileSync(new URL(f, here), 'utf8');\nconst ids = process.argv.slice(2).length ? process.argv.slice(2) : readdirSync(here).filter(f => f.endsWith('.html')).map(f => f.slice(0, -5)).sort();\nlet failed = 0;\nfor (const id of ids) {\n  const ctx = { console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error: console.error }, addEventListener() {}, location: { hash: '#' + id } };\n  ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);\n  try {\n    // the page's scripts, in its order: ../my-3d2dge.js, any asset set, then the kit's game\n    for (cons