{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghr7iZBdjo85u4RksrgK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now built everything the plan listed, so nothing from it is left out. The suite passes 120 of 120 checks and the AI Hub harness passes.\n\n**Added this round**\n- **Rendered fork:** a median island now grows out of the road toward each fork, with the two route arches over each half. Before, the fork was only the arches.\n- **Lens flare:** ghost discs run along the line from the sun through the screen centre, alongside the bloom pass from last round.\n- **Side-view start-line vignette:** before every Drive and Tour race, you see the car rolling in from the side while Bruno waves his flag. It can be skipped.\n\n**Checked in a real browser this round**\n- **Fork and vignette:** I looked at screenshots of both.\n- **Manual gearbox:** with a held key and the next-song button, first gear capped at 82 km/h and fourth gear reached 232.\n- **Versus second pad:** with two fake gamepads, only the second one pressed, player 2 drove and player 1 did not.\n- **Errors:** there were none.\n\nI didn't look at a screenshot of the flare or the manual-mode HUD on their own; both drew without errors.\n\n**`TASK.md` requirements:**\n- **Single bundled `.html`:** in the root.\n- **Dev mode:** in, with live sliders and a reset to defaults.\n- **Attract mode:** in.\n- **Hub multiplayer:** in, and the harness run is above.\n- **Controller-first UI:** PlayStation glyphs by default, with an Xbox option.\n- **Touch-only notice:** shown.\n- **No TODOs or placeholders:** the bundle lint finds none.\n- **`exit-interview.json`:** parses, every field is filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 04:21:40\n- Source: OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast\n- Plan: PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- Genre and Perspective: Arcade road racing (OutRun-style checkpoint racer) with a passenger-request layer (14 request types), a 14-postcard mission career, local two-player Versus and a seed garden for unlocks. Third-person chase camera on a pseudo-3D road (chase, high, bumper), with a side-view start-line vignette and 2D screens with portraits.\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff package, commit 4390a98) with E.Road, vanilla JavaScript on canvas 2D, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, Playwright 1.63.0 for browser checks only\n- Art Direction: Engine-native pixel art at 480x270, sunny pastel palette, scenery and cars drawn by code, Humanoid rig portraits, a stepped pixel-safe bloom and lens flare\n- Animation: The engine's Humanoid poses and expressions for portraits, plus code-driven car lean, slide angle and particles\n- Audio: No audio files. Seven generated songs, synthesised engine, horn and squeal sounds, and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- Online: AI Hub ghost session (protocol 1, 1 to 4 players); no other network use\n- Testing: Headless scripted playthroughs, real-browser keyboard and gamepad runs, screenshots for what scripts can't check, and the AI Hub conformance harness. No subagents or workflows.\n- Research: None beyond the engine docs, the ROAD kit, the plan and the AI Hub client\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (headless Chromium via Playwright)\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 12, including a boot failure from an undefined `clamp`, a first stage unfinishable inside the starting clock, missions with no verdict, a stale flag that stopped a second race from ending, and a crash drawing the time-out ending.\n- **Critical:** 4: the boot failure, the stale flag (a soft lock), missions that never ended, the time-out ending crash.\n- **Most helpful:** the scripted playthrough through the real scenes with held keys, then the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** the two-run determinism check, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the road module, backdrop presets, the standard pause, settings and controls shell, and headless `game.advance` for tests.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I assumed the pixel font could draw the PlayStation symbols and it drew \"?\". I also assumed the road could fork, and it can't.\n- **Most important thing built:** the race simulation, the pad, keyboard and mouse list menu, generated songs, babble voices, the dev panel and the split screen.\n- **Hardest part:** no continuous audio voice and no road branching.\n- **Engine changes:** controller symbols, arrows and a middle dot added to the pixel font; one comment reworded.\n- **One change:** a continuous audio voice with live pitch and volume.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the exact deliverables list, the concrete working rules, and a plan giving the game a strong spine and title.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was very large and didn't say which parts were required. The file-name pattern with the plan slug rule was tangled.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a very large plan into one session while still delivering a complete, polished slice.\n- **What I'd change:** mark each plan item required, nice to have or optional, and state the demo's target size."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":361379,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":617},"output_tokens":760,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"e2d027e2-900f-4a4e-9c3e-e7507e33904d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:57:55.128Z","request_id":"req_011Cghr7iBsEmQu7U4SiEa63"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML, exit-interview.json (parsed and filled), and all four feedback sections are present, but the every-feature condition is not shown as met. TASK.md asks for the Online and Attract features, a dev mode with live sliders, and a feature-complete, polished demo; the transcript shows these were built, but the TASK.md feature list was never checked item by item against the build. The final reply also lists gaps it never verified: it says it did not look at a screenshot of the lens flare or the manual-mode HUD, and the Testing Feedback calls the Engine's second-pad Versus check 'real-browser' while the earlier reply said it was not yet checked. The stop hook had already flagged the missing feature check twice. The reply also says 'Usage: unknown' and 'Tech' and 'Online' are stated without a verified feature checklist, so the stated completeness rests on the assistant's own summary rather than a demonstrated check against TASK.md."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"18f4d2fb-545a-40b2-b2fb-993e1cd3377f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:57:57.413Z","isSynthetic":true}
