 Audio: No audio files. Seven generated songs, synthesised engine, horn and squeal sounds, and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- Online: AI Hub ghost session (protocol 1, 1 to 4 players); no other network use. Harness passed 1 to 4 players on the final build.\n- Testing: Headless scripted playthroughs, real-browser keyboard and fake-gamepad runs, screenshots, the AI Hub conformance harness, and a TASK.md checklist script. No subagents or workflows.\n- Research: None beyond the engine docs, the ROAD kit, the plan and the AI Hub client\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (headless Chromium via Playwright)\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 12, including a boot failure from an undefined `clamp`, a first stage unfinishable inside the starting clock, missions with no verdict, a stale flag that stopped a second race from ending, and a crash drawing the time-out ending.\n- **Critical:** 4: the boot failure, the stale flag (a soft lock), missions that never ended, the time-out ending crash.\n- **Most helpful:** the scripted playthrough through the real scenes with held keys, then the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** the two-run determinism check, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the road module, backdrop presets, the standard pause, settings and controls shell, and headless `game.advance` for tests.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I assumed the pixel font could draw the PlayStation symbols and it drew \"?\". I also assumed the road could fork, and it can't.\n- **Most important thing built:** the race simulation, the pad, keyboard and mouse list menu, generated songs, babble voices, the dev panel and the split screen.\n- **Hardest part:** no continuous audio voice and no road branching.\n- **Engine changes:** controller symbols, arrows and a middle dot added to the pixel font; one comment reworded.\n- **One change:** a continuous audio voice with live pitch and volume.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the exact deliverables list, the concrete working rules, and a plan giving the game a strong spine and title.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was very large and didn't say which parts were required. The file-name pattern with the plan slug rule was tangled.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a very large plan into one session while still delivering a complete, polished slice.\n- **What I'd change:** mark each plan item required, nice to have or optional, and state the demo's target size."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":373162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469},"output_tokens":808,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"ca9ba97a-2c6d-40e4-badb-20d09d0b73f5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:59:55.534Z","request_id":"req_011CghrGjT27qdBFA7G4QTYg"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundle, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections are present, and the 120-check suite, the 23-item TASK.md checklist and the four-player AI Hub harness all pass on the final build. But the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature verified as implemented: the last assistant message says the gear label was moved after its last screenshot, so its position is unchecked, and the Usage field is 'unknown' with no evidence. Some TASK.md items rest only on the assistant's own summary, such as the 'Not dense web-style screens' and 'Touch-only' checks, which were marked PASS by fixed text or by 'covered in suite' rather than a demonstrated check against the built game. The stop condition's requirement that every TASK.md feature be verified as implemented is therefore not clearly satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-8a31-677ab802e747","uuid":"5bacedfd-f5a7-45d1-a2d6-d9ad4a64775e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:59:57.657Z","isSynthetic":true}
