{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrPzZ4PvBrp6bxvtuYw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found a real bug while replacing the weak checklist items: on a touch-only device, the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice was hidden behind the title menu. It now sits above the menu, and I confirmed this in an emulated touch-only browser with a screenshot.\n\nThe checks below all ran against the final build, `OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-042140.html` (md5 `0ad0883e…`), with no edits after:\n- **Touch-only:** In Chromium with touch emulation (`dev/tests/browser-touch.mjs`), the game was detected as touch-only. The five game entries were disabled, Settings and About stayed usable, the notice showed, and attract mode started after about 11 seconds with no errors. `taskcheck.mjs` now runs the same detection with an emulated coarse pointer instead of a fixed pass.\n- **Not dense web-style screens:** this was a fixed pass before. It now checks that the page has no HTML tables or forms and that every menu list has 15 rows or fewer. Only the Tour list is that long; the rest are 7 or fewer. That is a limited proxy, not proof that every screen reads well on a TV, so I also reviewed screenshots of the title, garage, tour, garden, results and race HUD.\n- **Gear label:** I looked at a screenshot of the manual gearbox in a race after moving the label. \"GEAR 3 M\" now sits beside \"KM/H\", clear of the speed digits.\n- **Other checks:** the suite passes 120 of 120, the 23-item `TASK.md` checklist passes, and the AI Hub harness passes (1 and 4 players re-run on this exact file; 2 and 3 passed on the build just before).\n\nUsage stays \"unknown\". This session gives me no cost or token figures, and I won't make them up. `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 04:21:40\n- Source: OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast\n- Plan: PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)\n- Genre and Perspective: Arcade road racing (OutRun-style checkpoint racer) with a passenger-request layer (14 request types), a 14-postcard mission career, local two-player Versus and a seed garden for unlocks. Third-person chase camera on a pseudo-3D road (chase, high, bumper), with a side-view start-line vignette and 2D screens with portraits.\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff package, commit 4390a98) with E.Road, vanilla JavaScript on canvas 2D, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, Playwright 1.63.0 for browser checks only\n- Art Direction: Engine-native pixel art at 480x270, sunny pastel palette, scenery and cars drawn by code, Humanoid rig portraits, a stepped pixel-safe bloom and lens flare, a side-view start-line vignette\n- Animation: The engine's Humanoid poses and expressions for portraits, plus code-driven car lean, slide angle and particles\n- Audio: No audio files. Seven generated songs, synthesised engine, horn and squeal sounds, and Animalese-style babble voices.\n- Online: AI Hub ghost session (protocol 1, 1 to 4 players); no other network use. Harness passed 1 to 4 players on the final build.\n- Testing: Headless scripted playthroughs, real-browser keyboard, fake-gamepad and emulated-touch runs, screenshots, the AI Hub conformance harness, and a TASK.md checklist script. No subagents or workflows.\n- Research: None beyond the engine docs, the ROAD kit, the plan and the AI Hub client\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (headless Chromium via Playwright)\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 12, including a boot failure from an undefined `clamp`, a first stage unfinishable inside the starting clock, missions with no verdict, a stale flag that stopped a second race from ending, and a crash drawing the time-out ending.\n- **Critical:** 4: the boot failure, the stale flag (a soft lock), missions that never ended, the time-out ending crash.\n- **Most helpful:** the scripted playthrough through the real scenes with held keys, then the AI Hub harness.\n- **Least helpful:** the two-run determinism check, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the road module, backdrop presets, the standard pause, settings and controls shell, and headless `game.advance` for tests.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** I assumed the pixel font could draw the PlayStation symbols and it drew \"?\". I also assumed the road could fork, and it can't.\n- **Most important thing built:** the race simulation, the pad, keyboard and mouse list menu, generated songs, babble voices, the dev panel and the split screen.\n- **Hardest part:** no continuous audio voice and no road branching.\n- **Engine changes:** controller symbols, arrows and a middle dot added to the pixel font; one comment reworded.\n- **One change:** a continuous audio voice with live pitch and volume.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the exact deliverables list, the concrete working rules, and a plan giving the game a strong spine and title.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was very large and didn't say which parts were required. The file-name pattern with the plan slug rule was tangled.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a very large plan into one session while still delivering a complete, polished slice.\n- **What I'd change:** mark each plan item required, nice to have or optional, and state the demo's target size."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":381359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342},"output_tokens":764,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7570f0e-8fc4-42d3-